+// ── CPS-2 WIDE v1: program ROM 4MB -> 6MB (docs/cps2_wide.md) ───────────
+// Descriptor-class change: only the mapped extent moves. Phase A/A1
+// measured zero vanilla reads into $400000-$5FFFFF across the whole legacy
+// corpus, so the newly-covered window shadows nothing live.
+//
+// The ROM range is declared FIRST and cps2_map() re-declares
+// $400000-$40000B as the CPS2 output registers afterwards; later entries
+// win in MAME, so the registers keep working exactly as on stock hardware.
+// The profile reserves $400000-$40000F, never allocate.
+//
+// NOTE, a real emulator-level divergence worth stating plainly: FBNeo maps
+// program ROM with SekMapMemory(CpsRom, 0, nCpsRomLen-1), which READ-shadows
+// those registers with ROM (writes still reach the handler), whereas MAME
+// keeps them readable. The reservation is what makes the difference
+// unobservable — no WIDE content may live there in either emulator.
+void cps2_state::cps2_wide_map(address_map &map)
+{
+	map(0x000000, 0x5fffff).rom();
+	cps2_map(map);
+}
+
+void cps2_state::decrypted_opcodes_wide_map(address_map &map)
+{
+	// Everything above $0FFFFF is outside the CPS-2 encryption window, so
+	// cps2_decrypt() copies it through verbatim (dec[a] = rom[a]) and the
+	// extension is plain in the opcode space too — extension content is
+	// authored RAW.
+	map(0x000000, 0x5fffff).rom().share(m_decrypted_opcodes);
+}
